From: HaeImAlan <me@haeimalan.com>
Date: Sun, 31 Aug 2026 02:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: validate nss before reporting an MCS rate to mac80211

ath11k_dp_rx_h_rate() copies rate_mcs and nss straight out of the RX
descriptor. It sets rx_status->encoding before validating anything, and
never checks nss at all, so a descriptor reporting nss == 0 produces an
rx_status that is marked HT/VHT/HE with nss == 0.

mac80211 rejects that in ieee80211_rx_list():

  WARNING: net/mac80211/rx.c:5043 ieee80211_rx_list
  Rate marked as a VHT rate but data is invalid: MCS: 0, NSS: 0

and drops the frame. On IPQ5018/QCN6122 this is reachable in normal
operation and the drop is followed by an oops in the ath11k RX path.

The HT case is worse than a warning: rate_idx is computed as
rate_mcs + (8 * (nss - 1)), so nss == 0 underflows and can produce an
out-of-range MCS index.

Validate mcs and nss together, and only mark the encoding once the
values are known good - a frame with unusable rate metadata is then
reported as legacy instead of being dropped.

The same unguarded code is present in ath11k upstream.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
@@ -2923,13 +2923,13 @@
 								is_cck);
 		break;
 	case RX_MSDU_START_PKT_TYPE_11N:
-		rx_status->encoding = RX_ENC_HT;
-		if (rate_mcs > ATH11K_HT_MCS_MAX) {
+		if (rate_mcs > ATH11K_HT_MCS_MAX || !nss || nss > 8) {
 			ath11k_warn(ar->ab,
-				    "Received with invalid mcs in HT mode %d\n",
-				     rate_mcs);
+				    "Received with invalid mcs/nss in HT mode %d/%d\n",
+				     rate_mcs, nss);
 			break;
 		}
+		rx_status->encoding = RX_ENC_HT;
 		rx_status->rate_idx = rate_mcs + (8 * (nss - 1));
 		if (sgi)
 			rx_status->enc_flags |= RX_ENC_FLAG_SHORT_GI;
@@ -2939,27 +2939,27 @@
 			rx_status->enc_flags |= RX_ENC_FLAG_LDPC;
 		break;
 	case RX_MSDU_START_PKT_TYPE_11AC:
-		rx_status->encoding = RX_ENC_VHT;
-		rx_status->rate_idx = rate_mcs;
-		if (rate_mcs > ATH11K_VHT_MCS_MAX) {
+		if (rate_mcs > ATH11K_VHT_MCS_MAX || !nss || nss > 8) {
 			ath11k_warn(ar->ab,
-				    "Received with invalid mcs in VHT mode %d\n",
-				     rate_mcs);
+				    "Received with invalid mcs/nss in VHT mode %d/%d\n",
+				     rate_mcs, nss);
 			break;
 		}
+		rx_status->encoding = RX_ENC_VHT;
+		rx_status->rate_idx = rate_mcs;
 		rx_status->nss = nss;
 		if (sgi)
 			rx_status->enc_flags |= RX_ENC_FLAG_SHORT_GI;
 		rx_status->bw = ath11k_mac_bw_to_mac80211_bw(bw);
 		break;
 	case RX_MSDU_START_PKT_TYPE_11AX:
-		rx_status->rate_idx = rate_mcs;
-		if (rate_mcs > ATH11K_HE_MCS_MAX) {
+		if (rate_mcs > ATH11K_HE_MCS_MAX || !nss || nss > 8) {
 			ath11k_warn(ar->ab,
-				    "Received with invalid mcs in HE mode %d\n",
-				    rate_mcs);
+				    "Received with invalid mcs/nss in HE mode %d/%d\n",
+				    rate_mcs, nss);
 			break;
 		}
+		rx_status->rate_idx = rate_mcs;
 		rx_status->encoding = RX_ENC_HE;
 		rx_status->nss = nss;
 		rx_status->he_gi = ath11k_he_gi_to_nl80211_he_gi(sgi);
